-- CONTROL for #1499: byte-structurally main.mdk -- same 2-module topology, same import,
-- same `data Box`, same interface with one method of the same type, same impl, same call
-- site. The ONE flipped feature: the interface method is named `size`, which collides
-- with no prelude standalone, so there is no shadowing and clause (b) owes nothing.
--
-- It must check clean (exit 0, zero diagnostics). If it breaks, multi-module
-- `check --json` broke in general -- NOT that #1499's owed warning landed.
--
-- Note this control is ALSO correct on `run` (exit 0, prints 3, hand-derived: `length`
-- of a 3-element list), which is what isolates #1492's run-only E-PANIC to the collision
-- itself rather than to anything else about this program's shape.
import helper.{threeItems}

interface Sized c where
  size : c -> Int

data Box = Box (List Int)

impl Sized Box where
  size (Box xs) = length xs

main = println (size (Box threeItems))
